# Copy to `.env` to override any of these. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Docker Compose reads `.env` from the directory holding docker-compose.yml, which is
# why both live at the repository root rather than under a compose/ subdirectory - in a
# subdirectory neither would be picked up automatically, which is the only reason to
# have them.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. This repository has none, and none is expected: the broker
# is unauthenticated by design (see SECURITY.md) and a KRaft cluster id is public by
# nature. The file exists so that the values which ARE configurable are visible and
# documented, rather than being buried as literals in the compose file.

# The KRaft cluster id. Fixed so cluster metadata stays valid across container restarts
# against the same named volume; regenerating it invalidates the existing log directory.
# Override only to run a second, separate cluster side by side.
#
# tests/contract/ asserts that the DEFAULT compiled into docker-compose.yml matches
# contracts/listeners.yaml. Overriding it here does not, and must not, change that.
CLUSTER_ID=GbUkriPcWUY1D0RM32nhAw
